Foundation.pm:263 and :281 check for the literal file .git/refs/karr/config to
detect a board. Loose refs get packed (git gc / git pack-refs), worktrees have
a gitdir indirection, and then the file does not exist although the ref does —
board silently skipped from the sweep.

FIX DIRECTION: use Git->ref_exists (libgit2, resolves packed refs) instead of
path existence. Found during architecture sweep. VERSION 0.304.
Fixed in ee4efbb: board detection now resolves refs/karr/config via libgit2 (Git->ref_exists) instead of the loose .git/refs/karr/config file, so packed-ref repos and worktrees are detected. New _is_karr_board_root guards the discovery loop against open_ext walk-up false positives. Regression tests in t/30-foundation.t (packed refs, worktree, walk-up guard, _process_repo) verified red->green. Full suite green (290 tests).
Review passed: libgit2 ref resolution + walk-up guard korrekt, Regressionstests (packed refs, worktree) vorhanden, Suite gruen.
